    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a natural extension of my curiosity—both a tool for problem-solving and a discipline that sharpens logical thinking. The abstract beauty in its structure appeals to me, but the highs are offset by moments where I see it as dry or intimidating, especially without connections to real-world applications. My extroverted nature means discussing math concepts with peers can make it more engaging.",
